  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14205687/assets/31fd7b63abbf8224421ee53b0703e9cc72fac2f9a8ffc3e460218bb42c4f229a.png)\n\nThe function $q(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[1,9].$ The graph of ${q}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $q(x),$ is shown above, where the area of the region between the graph and the $x$-axis is $12.$\n\nGiven that $q(9)=-1,$ what is the minimum value ${q}_{\\text{min}}$ of $q(x)$ on the interval $[1,9]?$\n\n${q}_{\\text{min}}=$\n{{field-1}}",
